["<aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>An evening on the couch with satellite imagery can save three wasted days of driving. Arrive with a plan A, a plan B and the wind for each.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 360\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map scouting funnel, wide at the top and narrow at the bottom: 1 pick the MU, 2 read your season rows, 3 keep only Crown land, 4 find south facing benches, 5 add edges and water, 6 trace roads and closures, 7 pin a glassing point and the wind. Out the bottom: plan A and plan B.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"360\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <path d=\"M10 10 L390 10 L370 50 L30 50 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"36\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">1 Pick the MU</text>\n    <path d=\"M32 54 L368 54 L348 94 L52 94 Z\" fill=\"#d3dcc4\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"80\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">2 Read your season rows</text>\n    <path d=\"M54 98 L346 98 L326 138 L74 138 Z\" fill=\"#c6d1b5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"124\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">3 Keep Crown land only</text>\n    <path d=\"M76 142 L324 142 L304 182 L96 182 Z\" fill=\"#b2c09c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"168\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">4 South benches</text>\n    <path d=\"M98 186 L302 186 L282 226 L118 226 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"212\" fill=\"#fff\">5 Edges, water</text>\n    <path d=\"M120 230 L280 230 L260 270 L140 270 Z\" fill=\"#6b7a50\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"256\" fill=\"#fff\">6 Roads, closures</text>\n    <path d=\"M142 274 L258 274 L240 314 L160 314 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"300\" fill=\"#fff\">7 Glass, wind</text>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"322\" width=\"160\" height=\"32\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"344\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Plan A and plan B</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Seven steps, wide to narrow. Run them before every trip.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: about this method</summary><ul><li>This session puts Maps 1, 2 and 3 together into one method you can run before every trip.</li><li>Example area: Region 3, around your Heffley Creek base. The method works anywhere in BC.</li><li>Acronyms here: <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"MU\">MU</button> (Management Unit), <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"FSR\">FSR</button> (Forest Service Road), GPS (Global Positioning System).</li><li>Every place on this page is a landscape type, not a named spot. You find the real spots on your own screen.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Use it for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Satellite imagery</td><td>Benches, edges, cutblocks (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Topo lines</td><td>Shape and steepness (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Land layers</td><td>Crown or private <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Synopsis\">Synopsis</button> page 34</td><td>Region 3 seasons <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>thompsonaccess maps</td><td>Closures <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Notebook or journal</td><td>Your marks (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Imagery can be years old. Check the image date (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: tools in full</summary><ul><li>Satellite imagery: any free imagery app or website, or the imagery layer in your hunting map app (Tip).</li><li>Topo lines on the same screen, or flip between topo and imagery (Tip). See Maps 1.</li><li>Land layers: iMapBC, iHunter Pro or BRMB PRO for Crown and private land (95%, see Maps 2 and 3).</li><li>The <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Synopsis\">Synopsis</button> Region 3 season table on page 34 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>The Region 3 closure maps at <a href=\"https://www.gov.bc.ca/thompsonaccess\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gov.bc.ca/thompsonaccess</a> (99%, synopsis page 33).</li><li>A notebook, or the app's hunt journal, for your marks and notes (Tip).</li><li>Imagery can be years old. A new cutblock or a burn may not show yet (Tip). Check the image date if the app shows it.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Season timeline chart for Region 3 deer, September to December, synopsis page 34. White tailed deer bucks: 10 September to 10 December. White tailed deer antlerless: 10 to 31 October. Mule deer bucks: 1 to 31 October. Mule deer 4 point bucks only: 1 November to 10 December. Units listed in the synopsis rows.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#dfe6d3\"><rect x=\"90\" y=\"30\" width=\"75\" height=\"220\"/><rect x=\"240\" y=\"30\" width=\"75\" height=\"220\"/></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"127\" y=\"24\">Sep</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"24\">Oct</text><text x=\"277\" y=\"24\">Nov</text><text x=\"352\" y=\"24\">Dec</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <text x=\"8\" y=\"62\" font-weight=\"bold\">Whitetail</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"78\">bucks</text>\n    <text x=\"8\" y=\"112\" font-weight=\"bold\">Whitetail</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"128\">antlerless</text>\n    <text x=\"8\" y=\"162\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mule deer</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"178\">bucks</text>\n    <text x=\"8\" y=\"212\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mule deer</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"228\">4 point only</text>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"114\" y=\"54\" width=\"225\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"190\" y=\"104\" width=\"52\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"165\" y=\"154\" width=\"75\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <rect x=\"240\" y=\"204\" width=\"100\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\"><text x=\"122\" y=\"71\">Sep 10 to Dec 10</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"171\">Oct</text></g>\n  <text x=\"246\" y=\"121\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Oct 10 to 31</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\">Nov 1 to Dec 10</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Region 3, synopsis page 34 (99%)</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The class is the rule, not just the date</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Pick the MU (Management Unit). Heffley Creek: MU 3-27 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Read your rows on page 34. Write the class beside each date.</li><li>Keep only <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Crown land\">Crown land</button>. Check in season changes online <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: steps 1 to 3 in full, with every season row</summary><ol><li><strong>Pick the MU.</strong> Heffley Creek sits in MU 3-27 (85%, read from the Region 3 map; see Maps 3).</li><li><strong>Read your rows on synopsis page 34.</strong> Find the MU in the \"Management Unit\" column for each species you hold a licence for.<ul><li>Mule deer bucks, 1 to 31 October, in 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44 and 3-46 (99%, page 34).</li><li>Mule deer 4 point bucks, 1 November to 10 December, same units (99%, page 34).</li><li>White tailed deer bucks, 10 September to 10 December, in 3-12 to 3-20 and 3-26 to 3-44 (99%, page 34).</li><li>White tailed deer antlerless, 10 to 31 October, in 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44 and 3-46 (99%, page 34).</li><li>Write the class (bucks, 4 point bucks, antlerless) next to each date. The class is the rule, not just the date.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Find the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Crown land\">Crown land</button>.</strong> Turn on the parcel layer. Shade out private land, reserves, parks and leases with cattle (see Maps 3).</li></ol><ul><li>In season changes are posted online. Check them before each trip (99%, synopsis page 7).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"What a bench looks like on satellite imagery: a dark band of timber across the top, below it a lighter, flatter patch with scattered single trees, then a steeper open slope below. The bench is circled in orange.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#b9a77f\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 0 L400 0 L400 90 C 300 110, 120 80, 0 100 Z\" fill=\"#33452c\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#33452c\"><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"104\" r=\"8\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"98\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"102\" r=\"9\"/><circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"96\" r=\"7\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M0 100 C 120 80, 300 110, 400 90 L400 190 C 300 200, 120 175, 0 190 Z\" fill=\"#d8cfa5\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#4d6340\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"140\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"160\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"130\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"350\" cy=\"130\" r=\"5\"/></g>\n  <ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"145\" rx=\"170\" ry=\"52\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"10 6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"8\" y=\"10\" width=\"150\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Dark timber</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"128\" width=\"160\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bench: light, flat</text>\n  <rect x=\"8\" y=\"232\" width=\"250\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"16\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Steeper open slope below</text>\n  <text x=\"16\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Scattered trees on the bench (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>South and southwest slopes, flat steps under timber (Tip).</li><li>October band near Heffley Creek: start about 700 to 1,200 m (Tip).</li><li>Snow comes: go lower <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: step 4 in full</summary><ul><li>Switch to satellite imagery over the Crown land you kept.</li><li>Look for <strong>south and southwest facing slopes</strong> (Tip). Interior mule deer winter range sits on south and west aspects in old Douglas fir (85%, Armleder 1994 via Hunt Mentor research notes).</li><li>Look for <strong>benches</strong>: flat steps on the slope. On topo, a wide gap between contour lines (90%, see Maps 1).</li><li>October search band near Heffley Creek: start at about 700 to 1,200 m (Tip, owner's working band). Valley floors here sit around 370 to 450 m (55%, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>A study near Kamloops used winter range below 760 m (80%, Willms 1976). So drop lower as snow comes.</li><li>Snow and cold, not the rut, push mule deer down to winter range (85%, Monteith 2011). Early snow: go lower. No snow: go higher (Tip).</li><li>On imagery, benches look like a lighter, flatter patch with scattered trees, under a darker band of timber (Tip).</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E8Otx9nyZgI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How To E-Scout For Whitetails: Key Terrain Features</b><small>Find saddles, benches and funnels on the map first.<br>onX Hunt, YouTube, 4 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three overlapping circles: bench, edge, and water. Where all three overlap is the star spot to mark on your map.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"120\" r=\"85\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"120\" r=\"85\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".35\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"200\" r=\"85\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".4\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"110\" y=\"95\">Bench</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"95\">Edge</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"262\">Water</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"110\" y=\"114\">flat step</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"114\">open meets cover</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"280\">pond, spring, creek</text></g>\n  <polygon points=\"200,128 207,146 226,146 211,157 217,176 200,165 183,176 189,157 174,146 193,146\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mark spots with all three (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Edge: open beside cover. Deer feed in the open, bed near cover <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Mark spots with bench, edge and water close together (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: step 5 in full</summary><ul><li><strong>Edges</strong> are where two kinds of cover meet: open grass beside timber, a young cutblock beside old trees, a burn beside green forest (Tip).</li><li>Deer feed in the open and bed close to cover. The edge is the doorway between them (60%, hunter observation).</li><li>A 5 to 15 year old cutblock against timber is classic deer country (60%, hunter observation; see Maps 3).</li><li><strong>Water:</strong> blue lines on topo, dark green strips on imagery, small ponds and springs on benches (Tip).</li><li>In a dry fall, water near a south bench makes it better (Tip).</li><li>Mark each spot that has all three: bench, edge, water within a short walk (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Route to a bench, traced from home: highway, then Forest Service Road, then spur road, to the last legal parking spot. A closure line blocks the spur beyond. From parking, a dashed foot route climbs about 40 minutes to the bench. Write the start time on your plan.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" opacity=\".7\"><path d=\"M200 0 C 260 60, 330 70, 400 60\"/><path d=\"M180 0 C 240 80, 320 100, 400 92\"/><path d=\"M160 0 C 220 100, 310 130, 400 124\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M0 270 L400 270\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\"/>\n  <path d=\"M60 270 C 80 220, 120 200, 160 190\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <path d=\"M160 190 C 190 180, 210 160, 230 150\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <path d=\"M230 150 C 250 140, 270 130, 300 126\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <path d=\"M236 132 L236 168\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <text x=\"244\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">closure</text>\n  <rect x=\"210\" y=\"140\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <text x=\"168\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Park here</text>\n  <path d=\"M220 140 C 230 110, 220 80, 260 50\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"290\" cy=\"42\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Bench</text>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">walk 40 min</text>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Highway</text>\n  <text x=\"90\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">FSR</text>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">spur</text>\n  <rect x=\"270\" y=\"196\" width=\"122\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"331\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dark climb?</text>\n  <text x=\"331\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Plan a start time</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Trace highway, FSR (Forest Service Road), spur, then on foot (Tip).</li><li>Check every road on the thompsonaccess closure maps <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Region 3: no motor vehicles above 1,700 m except on existing roads and trails <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: step 6 in full</summary><ul><li>Trace how you reach each spot: highway, FSR, spur road, then on foot (Tip).</li><li>Open the Region 3 closure maps at <a href=\"https://www.gov.bc.ca/thompsonaccess\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gov.bc.ca/thompsonaccess</a>. They are georeferenced PDF (Portable Document Format) maps (99%, synopsis page 33; see Maps 2).</li><li>Region 3: no motor vehicles, except snowmobiles, above 1,700 m, except on existing roads and trails (99%, synopsis page 33).</li><li>Check each road you plan to use with your ATV (all terrain vehicle) against the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Motor Vehicle Closed Area\">Motor Vehicle Closed Area</button> maps (99%, page 33).</li><li>Measure the walk from the last legal parking spot. Count contour lines on the climb (Tip, see Maps 1).</li><li>A spot that is a 40 minute climb in the dark needs a start time on your plan (Tip).</li><li>Leave gates as you find them. Region 3 asks this of every hunter (99%, synopsis page 33).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, side view at dawn. A draw lies between two slopes. Deer are on a bench on the right slope. The hunter walks up the left slope to a knob across the draw, 300 to 800 metres from the bench. Morning thermals rise up each slope, so the hunter's scent drifts up their own slope and away from the deer.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 80 L60 70 L110 110 L190 250 L210 250 L290 150 L330 150 L345 130 L400 60 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M190 250 L210 250\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">draw</text>\n  <text x=\"310\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bench</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(312 141)\"><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"-7\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\".85\">\n    <path d=\"M150 200 l-26 -40 m4 12 l-4 -12 l12 4\"><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-10 -16;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></path>\n    <path d=\"M250 200 l26 -40 m-12 4 l12 -4 l-4 12\"><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;10 -16;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" begin=\".5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></path>\n    <path d=\"M370 110 l14 -26 m-10 4 l10 -4 l-1 10\"><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;6 -12;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" begin=\".9s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></path>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: air rises up each slope</text>\n  <path id=\"hf-glass-point-path\" d=\"M150 200 L120 150 L100 112 L62 72\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/>\n  <g>\n    <path d=\"M0 0 L-24 -50 L16 -54 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".18\"/>\n    <circle r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <animateMotion dur=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#hf-glass-point-path\"/></animateMotion>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M70 60 L300 120\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"120\" y=\"58\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"185\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">300 to 800 m</text>\n    <text x=\"12\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Your knob</text>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"5.5s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"12\" y=\"200\" width=\"160\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"92\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Scent goes up your</text>\n    <text x=\"92\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">slope, not to deer</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Glass across the draw. Morning air carries scent up and away. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Pin a knob across the draw, 300 to 800 m (330 to 875 yd) from the bench (Tip).</li><li>Write one good wind and one bad wind per spot (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: step 7 in full</summary><ul><li>From each bench, look for a <strong>glassing point</strong> across or above it: a knob, a spur, a rock outcrop with a view (Tip).</li><li>Best: you look across a draw at the bench, 300 to 800 m (330 to 875 yd) away, so deer do not see or smell you (Tip).</li><li>Drop a pin on each glassing point, the parking spot and the bench. Name them A1, A2, B1 (Tip).</li><li>Plan the wind for each pin (see Wind and thermals):<ul><li>Mornings, air rises uphill <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Come in from above or the side.</li><li>Evenings, air sinks downhill <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Sit below or to the side.</li></ul></li><li>Write two lines per spot: \"Good wind: west. Bad wind: east.\" (Tip)</li><li>Check the forecast wind the night before and pick the spot that matches it (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"s2-map-scout\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:0\"><span>MU picked and confirmed on the Region 3 map</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:1\"><span>My species rows read on synopsis page 34, with the class written down</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:2\"><span>In season changes checked online</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:3\"><span>Crown land layer on, private land, reserves, parks and leases shaded out</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:4\"><span>South facing benches marked in my search band</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:5\"><span>Edges and water marked near each bench</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:6\"><span>Road route traced and checked against the thompsonaccess closure maps</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:7\"><span>Elevation of each road checked against the 1,700 m rule</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:8\"><span>Glassing point pinned for each bench</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:9\"><span>Good wind and bad wind written for each spot</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:10\"><span>Plan A and plan B chosen, offline maps downloaded</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-map-scout:11\"><span>Trip plan left with someone at home</span></label></div>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Mistake: on a morning hunt, the hunter sits below the bench on the same slope. Rising morning air carries the hunter's scent straight up to the bedded deer. Red cross: do not glass from below in the morning.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 280 L120 250 L250 120 L300 116 L400 30 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(280 106)\"><ellipse rx=\"14\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"290\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">bench</text>\n  <circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"236\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">You</text>\n  <path d=\"M140 226 C 180 190, 220 150, 262 118\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"256,112 270,112 264,126\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">rising air,</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">your scent</text>\n  <path d=\"M180 60 L230 110 M230 60 L180 110\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: never glass from below</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Scout with your thumb before you scout with your boots. But believe your boots.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Loving one bench before checking land, lease and road.</li><li>Reading the date, missing the class. A 2 point mule deer buck is not legal in November in Region 3.</li><li>A morning glassing point below the bench.</li></ul></aside>","<details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the mistakes in full</summary><ul><li>Falling in love with one bench and not checking whether it is Crown land, under a lease, or behind a closed road.</li><li>Reading the date on page 34 and missing the class: a 2 point mule deer buck is not legal in November in Region 3.</li><li>Pinning a glassing point that puts the morning thermal straight from you to the bench.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Pick three spots from home. Visit one. Compare the view with the imagery. Note what the map got wrong.</p></aside>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-02: page 7 (in season changes), page 33 (Region 3 access, 1,700 m rule, thompsonaccess, gates), page 34 (Region 3 seasons). 99%.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.gov.bc.ca/thompsonaccess\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Region 3 motor vehicle prohibition maps</a>, address read in the synopsis, page 33 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Map content not read here.</li></ul><ul><li>Hunt Mentor deer research notes, research/2026-10-01-deer.md: winter range aspect (Armleder 1994, 85%), migration trigger (Monteith 2011, 85%), Kamloops winter range study below 760 m (Willms 1976, 80%), valley elevations (55%, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul><ul><li>The 700 to 1,200 m band is the owner's working band, labelled Tip. Not a published figure.</li></ul>","<ul><li>Thermals: see Wind and thermals session sources <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Benches, edges, glassing points: hunter observation, labelled Tip or 60%.</li></ul>"]